---
import '../styles/global.css';
import { config } from '../lib/config';
const explorers = ['https://sepolia.etherscan.io/address/','https://etherscan.io/address/','https://basescan.org/address/','https://arbiscan.io/address/'];
---
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><title>PIT · Fee transparency</title></head><body><main class="shell"><header><a class="brand" href="../">pit<span>.</span></a><nav><a href="../">Trade</a><a href="../tools/">Toolbox</a><a href="../legal/">Legal</a></nav><span class="tag">{config.FEES_ENABLED ? "FEES ENABLED" : "FEES DISABLED"}</span></header><section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Nothing hidden</div><h1>What PIT earns.</h1><p>{config.FEES_ENABLED ? "Integrator fees are enabled. Review the configured rates below." : "Current integrator revenue: zero. FEES_ENABLED is false."}</p></section><div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>CoW swaps</h2><p>When enabled, the configured partner fee is {config.partnerFeeBps} basis points ({config.partnerFeeBps/100}%). It is included in signed appData under partnerFee with volumeBps and recipient. The quote shows the SDK's exact fee and minimum-receive amounts before signing.</p><p>Protocol fees and solver network costs are separate from PIT revenue. ERC20 approval gas is a separate wallet transaction. Unfilled orders do not earn PIT a partner fee.</p><p>Recipient: {config.feeRecipient||'Not configured — enabling fees will fail closed.'}</p>{config.feeRecipient&&explorers.map((url,i)=><p><a href={url+config.feeRecipient} rel="noreferrer">Recipient on {['Sepolia','Ethereum','Base','Arbitrum'][i]} ↗</a></p>)}</section><section class="panel"><h2>Hyperliquid perps</h2><p>When enabled, the default builder fee is {config.builderFeeTenthsBps} tenths of a basis point ({config.builderFeeTenthsBps/1000}%). The main wallet approves a maximum rate via EIP-712; each order includes its builder address and fee.</p><p>PIT enforces a perps cap of 100 tenths (10 bps). The helper caps spot at 1000 tenths (100 bps); spot trading is outside this release. Exchange fees and funding remain separate.</p><p>Builder: {config.builderAddress||'Not configured — no builder is sent while fees are off.'}</p>{config.builderAddress&&<a href={`https://app.hyperliquid-testnet.xyz/explorer/address/${config.builderAddress}`} rel="noreferrer">Builder address ↗</a>}</section></div><footer>No address analytics. Protocol APIs receive the account data required to quote and trade. <a href="../">Back to trading →</a></footer></main></body></html>
